# In-scope engagement targets. ONE CIDR OR IP PER LINE. Comments with #.
#
# This file is the authoritative scope boundary enforced by the kernel.
# It is not a wish list and not a reminder — if it is in here, the agent can reach it.
#
# Rules of thumb:
#   - Copy from the signed scope document, not from memory.
#   - Prefer /32 and /32 aggregates. Never a /16 "to be safe".
#   - Exclude shared infrastructure (load balancers, client cloud metadata, mail relays)
#     unless the client explicitly included it in writing.
#   - Put the client's own corporate ranges in here ONLY if they are in scope.
#
# Example:
# 203.0.113.10/32      # web app prod-facing
# 203.0.113.0/28       # staging cluster
# 198.51.100.0/28      # vpn egress range the client confirmed
